{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02699",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.68,
      "end_seconds": 6.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Come in, have a seat by the desk. How are things, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.56,
      "end_seconds": 12.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Well, I've been having my heart suddenly racing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.52,
      "end_seconds": 15.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.89,
      "end_seconds": 35.39,
      "duration_seconds": 17.5,
      "text": "Tiotropium inhaler. I take it once a day. I'm on paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed for the knee pain. Carvedilol, 6.25 milligrams, twice a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.51,
      "end_seconds": 40.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.34,
      "end_seconds": 44.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "It's been about two weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.81,
      "end_seconds": 48.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "mm, okay. Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.3,
      "end_seconds": 71.17,
      "duration_seconds": 20.87,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get it stopping just as suddenly as well. Actually, I've also been feeling lightheaded during an episode. I mean, the it stopping just as suddenly? That's been for about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.71,
      "end_seconds": 83.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "And fainting, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.53,
      "end_seconds": 87.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Nope, uh, no fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.86,
      "end_seconds": 93.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "have you had any breathlessness, family history of sudden death or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.26,
      "end_seconds": 98.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "no, uh, I'd have said so"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.72,
      "end_seconds": 103.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Right, how are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.88,
      "end_seconds": 107.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.19,
      "end_seconds": 111.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "right, is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.39,
      "end_seconds": 116.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "No, you know, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.31,
      "end_seconds": 119.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.38,
      "end_seconds": 130.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Tramadol. I come out in... well, feeling very drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.78,
      "end_seconds": 134.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Right, does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.34,
      "end_seconds": 137.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "My cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.38,
      "end_seconds": 144.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Okay, anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.76,
      "end_seconds": 160.12,
      "duration_seconds": 14.36,
      "text": "COPD, for nearly five years. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it. I told my wife I'd come today. I have arthritis in my knees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.47,
      "end_seconds": 162.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.66,
      "end_seconds": 166.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Heart failure, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.07,
      "end_seconds": 176.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Alright, COPD and arthritis in your knees, that that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.09,
      "end_seconds": 189.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "let's talk a little about your daily life and habits"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.44,
      "end_seconds": 201.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.17,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning. My partner and our baby. I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.32,
      "end_seconds": 204.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.72,
      "end_seconds": 216.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.67,
      "end_seconds": 242.47,
      "duration_seconds": 15.8,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 75 beats a minute, height 182 centimetres, temp 36.9 degrees, BP is 113 over 81, weight 89 kilos, BMI works out to 26.9, saturation 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.27,
      "end_seconds": 249.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.32,
      "end_seconds": 263.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.8,
      "end_seconds": 269.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.33,
      "end_seconds": 289.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Your heart sounds and rhythm are normal today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.7,
      "end_seconds": 306.75,
      "duration_seconds": 14.05,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Right, here's what I'm thinking. The most likely explanation is episodes of supraventricular tachycardia. I can't rule out atrial fibrillation yet. We should do a thyroid test for palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 308.37,
      "end_seconds": 313.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "We have a slot Tuesday at 11:30 am, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.78,
      "end_seconds": 317.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Tuesday, that works for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.82,
      "end_seconds": 345.43,
      "duration_seconds": 26.61,
      "text": "I'm sending you for a 7-day heart monitor because of paroxysmal palpitations. An ECG is what I'd like next, for palpitations. Try blowing hard against a closed mouth and nose when it starts. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. I think the cardiology clinic should see you too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.39,
      "end_seconds": 350.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "sure, um, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.05,
      "end_seconds": 358.21,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "Let's plan a check after the monitor. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.16,
      "end_seconds": 362.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "I think I understand everything thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.44,
      "end_seconds": 364.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}